 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Welcome. Think birthday without God. Start with candles and cake, of course. Partner does the blessing and lighting, each guest with a single candle before dinner. Then everyone sings as the candles light the room. Then you light them all one at a time. Put a small box of salt and pepper between the plate and the cake. It plays the same function as the candles without any specific words. And if space is an issue, you can cut down on it completely and just use the cake and candles. A few well chosen words still carry a lot.",
